    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\n`checkDigit` is a derived field on the owner response, computed as a single Luhn check digit over the digits of `customerCode`. Following the existing pattern for other derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipLevel`, etc.), I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (read-only `integer`, 0\u20139), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` and a `checkDigit(Owner)` method implementing the standard Luhn algorithm over the digits of `customerCode` (ignoring the hyphen separators), matching the spec exactly. It returns `null` when `customerCode` is absent.\n\nThe mapper runs in the responder (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and on fetch, so both POST and GET responses now carry the value. `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` \u2014 which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit \u2014 passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS` confirms the suite is green.",
